WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000 line:0
[On-screen text: Why did you choose QC?]

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:08.310
It allows me to work virtually from home while I get to do other things. So, it

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.790
was able to fit within my schedule.

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:14.470
I could work at the coursework when it was convenient for me.

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:19.510
I really liked the organized and structured course outline.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:23.109
I like the fact that QC provides the opportunity for us to do the work at our

00:00:23.119 --> 00:00:26.190
own pace, so we don't feel like we're rushing to get assignments done or

00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:27.750
to get quizzes done.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:31.750
I chose QC because I wanted something that was flexible and allowed me to work at my own pace.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:37.910
Now that I'm building my business and I have clients and I still have a life.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.590
I have friends and family and all that stuff.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:46.110
I'm still able to sit down and say, "Okay, I have 2 hours. I can pick away at it for

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.389
two hours and then I can leave it for a week and I can come back to it,"

00:00:48.399 --> 00:00:50.630
and that has just been amazing.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:53.670
Actually, I really like the flexibility of being able to complete the courses

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:56.500
and the assignments really at your own pace.

00:00:56.510 --> 00:00:59.310
They were more than helpful. I mean, they guided me in the right direction.

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.990
They were telling me exactly what I had to do to answer the question on a particular assignment.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.750
And I was also able to reach out to some of the students within the virtual community

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.500
groups and they were also helpful.

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:14.390
Everybody is so nice and so helpful. And I'm so grateful for QC Design School.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.429
I'm part of the virtual community now, which is so fun to meet people from all

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:24.149
over the world, surrounding myself with people who are like-minded and in the

00:01:24.159 --> 00:01:24.800
same kind of industry.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:28.230
Enrolling in those courses ultimately gave me

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:33.109
the sound knowledge base and the foundation I needed for interior decorating,

00:01:33.119 --> 00:01:39.190
but it also really gave me the confidence I needed to launch my own business.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.749
QC has helped get me where I am today in owning three businesses, a calligraphy

00:01:43.759 --> 00:01:47.190
business, an interior decor business, and The Friendly Market, which is

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:49.590
something I started with a fellow QC graduate.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.590
The most rewarding part has been giving me
the confidence to say I can totally

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.030
do this. I never thought that I could do it

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.270
professionally and make a job out of it.
And I think having the support of the

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:06.310
staff and having the course material was
like my stepping stone to being like,

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:08.710
okay, I really could make something out
of this.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.910
I am so grateful for my experience and

00:02:10.920 --> 00:02:14.270
everything I've learned at QC Design School
because I am applying everything

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:18.000
to my current job today.

